# Fix rounds run targeted tests: a seat rule in every producer and critic charter, and a plan check in dispatch that refuses a fix-round plan asking for a full-suite run. Owner question 2026-09-14 09:00: is this permanent or session only. 2026-09-14
#
# DISPATCH: ./scripts/dispatch.sh git@github.com:Arlencho/dev-agents.git wave-plans/dev-agents/2026-09-14-fix-round-test-budget.plan --detach --retries 1
# Why: a one-line fix (PR 89 round 4) took 52 minutes because the seat ran the full 423-test desk suite about four times, including a self-made mutation run, and waited on a backgrounded run; the plan text asked for the full suite.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1 | web-frontend | Branch feat/fix-round-test-budget from origin/main. Layer 2, seat instructions: add one rule block, identical text, to every producer charter (roles/go-backend.md, web-frontend.md, db-architect.md, api-designer.md, devops.md, test-engineer.md, mobile.md, docs-writer.md) and the matching provider agent copies under providers/*/agents where they exist: In a fix round (a plan whose header or task names a round number above 1, or a FIX-ROUND header, or a fix suffix), run only the test file or test names that cover the code you touched, plus the failing tests the critic wrote; do not run the full suite, do not run mutation checks, do not background a test run and wait on it; the full suite runs once, in the final round before merge, or in CI. Add the matching rule to every critic charter (backend-critic, frontend-critic, database-critic, api-critic, plan-critic, devops-critic, security-reviewer): In a review round above 1, re-run only the fixtures of the findings being closed plus one regression check you name; do not re-run every fixture from earlier rounds unless the diff touches their code. Layer 1, a mechanical check: scripts/dispatch.sh (or the plan parser it uses) warns and stops before starting when a plan is a fix round and any task line contains a full-suite VERIFY (make test, the whole tests directory runner, or the words full suite) without the words final round; the stop message names the task line and the rule; an explicit header ALLOW-FULL-SUITE lets the owner override. Tests in tests/run-routing-tests.sh or a new tests/run-plan-check-tests.sh: every producer and critic charter carries its rule block verbatim; a fix-round plan with make test is refused; the same plan with ALLOW-FULL-SUITE passes; a round 1 plan with make test passes. Document the rule in README next to the plan format. VERIFY: run tests/run-plan-check-tests.sh (or the routing test file you extended) only; this round may run make test once at the end because it changes the dispatcher. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open a draft PR titled Fix rounds run targeted tests: seat rule and plan check. | feat/fix-round-test-budget

2 | plan-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the PR on branch feat/fix-round-test-budget. No commits, no push, no review, no labels; tmp writes only. Record head SHA at start and at report. Check: the rule block is present and identical in every producer and critic charter including provider copies; the plan check refuses a fix-round plan with a full-suite VERIFY, passes it with the override header, and never refuses a round 1 plan; the check cannot be bypassed by lower case or by a VERIFY split across lines; the stop message names the task line. Post ONE comment on the PR whose first line reads CRITIC FIX ROUND TEST BUDGET with SAFE-TO-MERGE, BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE and citations. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash, no AI tool or vendor name. | feat/fix-round-test-budget
